From: captain <captain@lcars.local>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 18:54:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/8] Pinefeat CEF: end a Busy move or calibration when the
 state can't be read

A move sets the absolute (and relative) position Busy, and an accepted
CALIBRATE sets the absolute position and FOCUS_MAX Busy. Only
updateProperties() ends them, and TimerHit() calls it only when `f`, `r`,
`d` and `a` all answer once `e` reports the focuser still. A lens
removed, or a controller that can't read it (`f` answering `nc`), left
them Busy for ever: a client waiting for the end of the move or of the
calibration waited for ever too.

Once `e` reports the focuser still, a read that fails now turns each of
these properties that is still Busy to Alert. A successful read ends
them as before.
---
 drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp b/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
index afdb1dc..5b2da96 100644
--- a/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
+++ b/drivers/focuser/pinefeat_cef.cpp
@@ -489,6 +489,28 @@ void PinefeatCEF::TimerHit()
         {
             updateProperties(pos, max, dist, aper);
         }
+        else
+        {
+            // Stopped, and the state can't be read (no lens, a fault): a move or a calibration still Busy has
+            // failed. Only a successful read ends it otherwise.
+            if (FocusAbsPosNP.getState() == IPS_BUSY)
+            {
+                FocusAbsPosNP.setState(IPS_ALERT);
+                FocusAbsPosNP.apply();
+            }
+
+            if (FocusRelPosNP.getState() == IPS_BUSY)
+            {
+                FocusRelPosNP.setState(IPS_ALERT);
+                FocusRelPosNP.apply();
+            }
+
+            if (FocusMaxPosNP.getState() == IPS_BUSY)
+            {
+                FocusMaxPosNP.setState(IPS_ALERT);
+                FocusMaxPosNP.apply();
+            }
+        }
     }
 
     SetTimer(getCurrentPollingPeriod());
